    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d438">

                <pb facs="0409" n="399" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg399"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/333: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Thailand</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-02-05T19:00:00+07:00">February 5, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 5—1:16 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>67. Referring to the Legation’s telegram No. 125, Octohber 17, 6 p.m., and to the
                    Department’s telegram No. 70, October 23, 5 p.m.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d438-f1"/>
                    In view of the recent political developments which, as I have indicated in my
                    telegrams, may place Thailand definitely under Japanese domination <pb
                        facs="0410" n="400" xml:id="pg400"/> within the very near future I request
                    telegraphic instructions regarding the advisability of the evacuation of
                    American women and children from this area before it is too late, especially in
                    view of the isolated position of this country and the consequent difficulties of
                    evacuating in the event of a sudden emergency. The British Minister<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d438-f2"/> and I have held frequent consultations regarding this
                    matter. Our views in this matter coincide. He is requesting instructions from
                    his Government.</p>
                <p>Sent to Cavite for repetition to the Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
